  "body": "LOT-082 follow-up (no lot)\nCloses #875\nClaim: mac/M1\n\n**Merge:** by the core orchestrator or the maintainer (AGENTS.md §8): the PR adds a public `HFRModels` type (`SubforumTarget`).\n\n**Problem.** Inside a sub-forum there is no Tous / Favoris / Suivis / Lus filter. #427 only did categories, because the app knows a sub-forum by its path only.\n\n**Cause.** HFR filters a sub-forum with the category list URL plus `subcat=<s>` (`R603d`), and the home links give no id. The sub-forum's page names its category and subcat in the `md_btn_new_topic` link (`R06`: own page, logged out; `R603d`: filtered page, logged in). A category page does not (`R09`).\n\n**Change.**\n- `SubforumTarget` (HFRModels) reads cat and subcat from `newTopicPath`.\n- `topicList` takes an optional `subcategory`. With it, the request is `R603d`'s exact query; a category keeps its short form.\n- `TopicListModel` loads the sub-forum page, learns the target, then asks for the stored choice with `subcat=<s>&owntopic=<n>`.\n- The filter is offered only once the id is known. Logged out stays on Tous.\n- No REST dependency (#873).\n- `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md`: the R2 row and the §6c bullet.\n\n**Tests.**\n- `SubforumTargetTests`: fixtures `R603d`, `R06`, `R09`, plus malformed paths.\n- `HFREndpointReadTests`: `topicListOfASubforumIsTheCapturedR603dUrl` (exact string) and `topicListOfASubforum` (long-form variants).\n- Four `TopicFilterTests` cases: filtered at first load; reload and paging with subcat; page names none; logged out.\n- Full iPhone and iPad suites pass.\n\n**Pending capture.**\n- The sub-forum's own page, logged in.\n- A page where the viewer may not post.\n- An empty sub-forum.\n- The filtered URL with an expired cookie.\n\n### Ledger\n\n```gap-edit\nGAP-023\nSwiftHFR final: Segmented Tous / Favoris / Suivis / Lus on a category's list and on a sub-forum's, persisted under the legacy key; a sub-forum is filtered with the `subcat` its own page names in the new-topic link, so its filter starts after its first page and is not offered when the page names none; logged out, only Favoris, Suivis and Lus are disabled (Tous stays, and a tap on a disabled one never overwrites the stored choice); a Favoris section title opens its category on Favoris (#427, #593, #875).\nSource: #427, #875\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJ1auuPWv2FeT7Q4Ps\n",
