   "body": "**Adversarial review round 2 (Opus 5.5) — APPROVE** — head ed5b1d31 (round 1: REQUEST CHANGES at 77d392df)\n\n1. **nit** — `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/ForumScopeBar.swift:50`: a category opened by path (`ForumListModel.swift:50`) is a `.subforum` whose page names no `subcat`; its note still tells the user to choose « Tous les sous-forums » while on that list. Optional: show the note on real sub-forum rows only, or drop the second clause. « Tous » still loads.\n\nRound-1 findings:\n- 1 resolved: the sub-forum request is `R603d.meta.json:6`'s `url` exactly, only cat/page/subcat/owntopic varying; no subcategory keeps the short form (`topicListDefaultsToFirstPageOfAllTopics`); `topicListOfASubforumIsTheCapturedR603dUrl` fails against the round-1 form.\n- 2 resolved: longest changed Swift line 138 (`PageFetcher.swift:30`).\n- 3, 4, 5 resolved (§6c sources split, doc comment, expired-cookie capture pending).\n- 6 mostly resolved (see 1 above). 7 resolved (merge by the core orchestrator).\n- 8 resolved: the gap-edit is well formed; `Source` is a replaceable column (`tooling/docs/README.md:42`, `ledger.py:18`); the new cell matches the code.\n\nBranch-wide: nothing broken (own path for « Tous » and the first load, target kept when a filtered page has no link, failed or superseded loads leave `subforumTarget`, `subcategory: nil` for categories).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
